 "words": "It’s Phil. I’m in Pittsburgh. I’m not moving the couch.",
 "intention": "Sever the emotional anchor to the loop by explicitly abandoning the task that defined my previous failure, forcing a new variable into the Tuesday equation.","detail": "I walk to the nearest payphone, insert the coins I carried in my pocket, and dial. I do not ask if she is busy. I do not ask for the van time. I simply state the location and the refusal. This is not a promise; it is a severance. The loop is a reaction to my desire to fix the past through a specific physical act. By refusing the act while already present, I break the causal link between my arrival and my obligation. If I do not move the couch, I do not move the couch. The variable changes."
